From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: matisse3g: use register backlight control

Use the populated LP8556's supported register-only brightness mode,
keeping the existing Matisse current/channel configuration unchanged. A
stopped CAMSS GP0 PWM clock cannot guarantee the output level needed for
darkness. Register brightness and BL_CTL provide an explicit off state
instead.

Connect the firmware framebuffer to this backlight so DRM screen-off and
system suspend can disable illumination through the existing LP855x
driver. Disable the unused PWM adapter. No GPIO wiring assumptions are
introduced.

Reference: TI LP8556 SNVS871 Device Control BRT_MODE=10 and BL_CTL;
captured SM-T531 LP8556 at I2C address 0x2c; existing Matisse common DTS
configuration.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
@@ -89,6 +89,7 @@
 };
 
 &framebuffer0 {
+	backlight = <&lcd_backlight>;
 	clocks = <&mmcc MDSS_AHB_CLK>,
 		 <&mmcc MDSS_AXI_CLK>,
 		 <&mmcc MDSS_BYTE0_CLK>,
@@ -449,3 +450,18 @@
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+/ {
+	i2c-backlight {
+		lcd_backlight: backlight@2c {
+			/* Register-only control has a defined off state. */
+			dev-ctrl = /bits/ 8 <0x85>;
+			/delete-property/ pwms;
+			/delete-property/ pwm-names;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&backlight_pwm {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
-- 
